WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.903 --> 00:00:04.320
MEGAN LACY: I
started at Hillsdale

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.030
when I was 16 years old.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.640
I think that's one of the
reasons my parents were

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.005
pleased to have me at a
small school close to home.

00:00:12.005 --> 00:00:13.380
Everyone at
Hillsdale immediately

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.330
is overwhelmingly
kind and welcoming,

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:18.485
and it's a family atmosphere
from the beginning.

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.860
And so I think
that it's probably

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.900
one of the few colleges
I could have gone to

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.930
at that time that would
have felt so safe.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.520
I studied a lot in college.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.410
I think I might have
studied more in college

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.570
than I did in law school.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.000
I grew up figure
skating competitively,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.270
and so I trained
like a full time job.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.558
And I think that it was kind
of natural to approach college

00:00:39.558 --> 00:00:42.100
with a similar attitude that if
you're going to do something,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.408
you do it seriously.

00:00:43.408 --> 00:00:44.700
I'm grateful for that attitude.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.473
I'm grateful to my
parents for putting up

00:00:46.473 --> 00:00:47.640
with all of that growing up.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.460
I think it was a gift to me.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.190
I was a Kappa,
which was great fun.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.800
Several of my sorority
sisters remain dear friends

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.630
to this day.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.940
After law school, I clerked
for two federal judges,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:02.130
one on a federal
district court and one

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.220
on the United States Court of
Appeals for the Ninth Circuit.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.980
When Justice Kavanaugh
was nominated,

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.320
I went to work in the White
House Counsel's office

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.150
to assist them.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.090
I spent a lot of time
with the justice,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.752
and I was delighted
when he asked

00:01:16.752 --> 00:01:18.210
if I would be
interested in working

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.592
for him at the court
after his confirmation.

00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:22.800
Clerking at the Supreme
Court is an incredible honor.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.140
It is a dream for
many law students.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.640
It was for me.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.160
There are only a
few dozen people

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.170
who get to do it every year.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.890
Hillsdale is a very special
place to spend four years.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.237
I would tell students to
appreciate the gift that they

00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:40.320
have and the education
that they're being offered.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.930
It is rare.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.610
Take advantage of
your professors.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.740
Take advantage of the
community and the friendships

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.740
that you can build at the
school, and work hard.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.700
Don't take it for granted
is what I would say.

